/-!
# The even SL₃ critical pair: field lines and alignment

The original normalizer action is semilinear through the full SL₃ marking.
A nontrivial field-twisted involution has more than q displacements, including
over F₄. Consequently a nonzero commutator of order at most q is a genuine
field line. The source adapter applies this in both orientations of the
critical pair and uses actual line transitivity to correct g on the right.

The normal two-core acts trivially on V/V₁ by the irreducible natural SL₂
quotient action. This proves the point-core bound and closes the SL₃ branch,
including the reciprocal field line and odd-distance conclusion. Only the
genuine earlier marking, flag, fixed-space and amalgam inputs remain explicit.
The final K=L₁ assembly belongs to qt-d-1222-natural-closure-amalgam.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.5.8, refs/quasithin.pdf, printed p.784.
-/
